Stack Pattern

 LIFO - Last In First Out

 All operations of stack is O(n)


Where Stack is Used
- Very common in interviews:
- Parentheses validation
- Next Greater Element
- Monotonic stack
- Undo/Redo
- Expression evaluation
- Largest rectangle in histogram
- Daily Temperatures
--------------------------------------
A Monotonic Stack is a stack that always remains in a specific order:

Monotonic Increasing Stack → elements increase (small → big)
Monotonic Decreasing Stack → elements decrease (big → small)

We pop elements that break this order.